{"id":"consultant-clients","title":"Who pays the permit consultants","question":"Who is paying to get permits through, and do organizations funded by the City pay too?","finding":"164 companies and organizations are named as paying clients on the consultants' filings; 9 of them are nonprofits the City itself funds, which between them were reported as paying $1,002,057 in permit-consulting fees. A further 307 clients are private owners, counted here but not named.","how":"Client names and 'amount of compensation' from the readable quarterly Form 3410B filings, summed by client. A client is marked City-funded when its name matches a nonprofit in the City's payment records.","limits":"For an affordable-housing builder, hiring a consultant is an ordinary project cost. The point is where the money goes: when a City-funded builder must pay a specialist to get a City permit, part of the public grant is spent on the City's own process. Name matching is by exact normalised name and is not proof of identity; fees are a floor for the reasons given above.","tier":"OFFICIAL","columns":[{"k":"client","t":"Client named on the filing","type":"org"},{"k":"cityFunded","t":"Nonprofit funded by the City","type":"text"},{"k":"cityPaid","t":"City payments to it since FY2019","type":"usd"},{"k":"fees","t":"Consulting fees reported","type":"usd"},{"k":"quarters","t":"Quarterly entries","type":"int"},{"k":"consultant","t":"Mostly paid to","type":"org"},{"k":"years","t":"Years","type":"text"}],"rows":[{"client":"Mercy Housing California","clientKey":"MERCY HOUSING CALIFORNIA","cityFunded":"Yes","cityPaid":28212026,"fees":615615,"quarters":34,"consultant":"Dale Durrett","years":"2018–2026"},{"client":"Chinatown Community Development Center","clientKey":"CHINATOWN COMMUNITY DEVELOPMENT CENTER","cityFunded":"Yes","cityPaid":56308756,"fees":241085,"quarters":14,"consultant":"Dale Durrett","years":"2020–2026"},{"client":"Mission Housing Development Corp.","clientKey":"MISSION HOUSING DEVELOPMENT"